===Etymology===
From {{der|en|frm|manœuvre||manipulation, maneuver}} and {{m|frm|manouvrer||to maneuver}}, from {{der|en|fro|manovre||handwork, manual labor}}, from {{der|en|la-med|manopera}}, {{m|la|manuopera||work done by hand, handwork}}, from {{m|la|manu||by hand}} + {{m|la|operari||to work}}. First recorded in the Capitularies of Charlemagne (800 AD) to mean "chore, manual task", probably as a calque of the {{der|en|frk|*handuwerk||hand-work}}. Compare {{cog|ang|handweorc}}, {{cog|ang|handġeweorc}}, {{cog|de|Handwerk}}. The verb is a doublet of the verb {{doublet|en|manure|notext=1}}.

