{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make (something) [[smaller]] or as small as possible; [[shrink]]; [[reduce]].
#: {{syn|en|besmall|smallify|Thesaurus:diminish}}
#: {{ant|en|maximize}}
#: {{ux|en|We have to '''minimize''' the budget.}}
#: {{ux|en|Try to '''minimize''' your biases.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Willard Price|title=Roving South, Rio Grande to Patagonia|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=J. Day Co.|year=1948|page=13|oclc=1358700|passage=Terry, author of the indispensable ''Terry's Guide to Mexico'', has a name for it&nbsp;– atrabiliousness. "The defect of many of the murals," he says, speaking of those in the orphan asylum, "is the facial atrabiliousness of some of the subjects. To the observer it '''minimizes''' the grandeur of the conception {{...}}"}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1954|title=Instruments and Control Systems - Volume 27  |author= |page=1466 |ISBN= |passage=For accurate stopping, the drive must incorporate means for '''minimizing''' inertia overdrift.  }}
#* {{quote-book|en|2023|Jacqueline B. Helfgott|Copycat Crime|passage=One way to '''minimize''' or mitigate the copycat effect is to deemphasize the perpetrator and deglorify the violence in real and fictional stories.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[relegate]] or [[assign]] (something) to a less insignificant status; [[diminish]].
#: {{syn|en|lessen|lower|reduce|Thesaurus:diminish}}
#: {{ux|en|The insurance adjuster tried to '''minimize''' the extent of the damage to [[lessen]] the company's exposure to liability.}}
# {{lb|en|computing|transitive|graphical user interface}} To remove (a [[window]]) from the main display area, collapsing it to an [[icon]] or [[caption]].
#: {{ant|en|maximize}}
#: {{ux|en|I didn't close anything, but I '''minimized''' all the windows so I could see the desktop.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To treat (someone) in a [[slighting]] manner.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1993|author=Jan McDaniel|title=One Golden Summer|page=95|text={{...}} father who had never openly '''minimized''' him or anything he did {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To treat as [[trivial]] or [[insignificant]]; to [[trivialize]].
#: {{syn|en|banalize|disparage|play down|Thesaurus:trivialize}}
#: {{ux|en|to '''minimize''' someone's feelings}}

